{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class textdocumentanalysis {\n    static int countInsideBraces = 0, longestWord = 0;\n\n    public static int countWords(String str) {\n        str = str.replaceAll(\"_\", \" \");\n        str = str.trim().replaceAll(\"\\\\s+\", \" \");\n        String[] words = str.split(\" \");\n        if (words.length == 1 && words[0].isEmpty()) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        return words.length;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = scanner.nextInt();\n        scanner.nextLine(); // consume newline\n        String input = scanner.nextLine();\n        \n        List<Integer> bracePositions = new ArrayList<>();\n        bracePositions.add(-1);\n        \n        for (int idx = 0; idx < input.length(); idx++) {\n            char ch = input.charAt(idx);\n            if (ch == '(' || ch == ')') {\n                bracePositions.add(idx);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int pairIndex = 1;\n        int wordCountInside = 0;\n        int maxWordLength = 0;\n        StringBuilder outsideText = new StringBuilder();\n        \n        while (pairIndex < bracePositions.size() - 1) {\n            int openPos = bracePositions.get(pairIndex);\n            int closePos = bracePositions.get(pairIndex + 1);\n            \n            String insideContent = input.substring(openPos + 1, closePos);\n            wordCountInside += countWords(insideContent);\n            \n            String outsideSegment = input.substring(bracePositions.get(pairIndex - 1) + 1, openPos);\n            outsideText.append(\"_\").append(outsideSegment);\n            \n            pairIndex += 2;\n        }\n        \n        String finalOutsideSegment = input.substring(bracePositions.get(bracePositions.size() - 1) + 1);\n        outsideText.append(\"_\").append(finalOutsideSegment);\n        \n        String cleanedOutside = outsideText.toString()\n                .replaceAll(\"_\", \" \")\n                .trim()\n                .replaceAll(\"\\\\s+\", \" \");\n        \n        String[] outsideWords = cleanedOutside.split(\" \");\n        for (String word : outsideWords) {\n            if (word.length() > maxWordLength) {\n                maxWordLength = word.length();\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.print(maxWordLength + \" \" + wordCountInside);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef count_words(s):\n    s = s.replace(\"_\", \" \")\n    s = s.strip().replace(\"\\\\s+\", \" \")\n    words = s.split(\" \")\n    if len(words) == 1 and words[0] == \"\":\n        return 0\n    return len(words)\n\ndef main():\n    input_lines = []\n    for line in sys.stdin:\n        input_lines.append(line.strip())\n    \n    n = int(input_lines[0])\n    input_str = input_lines[1]\n    \n    brace_positions = [-1]\n    \n    for idx in range(len(input_str)):\n        ch = input_str[idx]\n        if ch == '(' or ch == ')':\n            brace_positions.append(idx)\n    \n    pair_index = 1\n    word_count_inside = 0\n    max_word_length = 0\n    outside_text = []\n    \n    while pair_index < len(brace_positions) - 1:\n        open_pos = brace_positions[pair_index]\n        close_pos = brace_positions[pair_index + 1]\n        \n        inside_content = input_str[open_pos + 1:close_pos]\n        word_count_inside += count_words(inside_content)\n        \n        outside_segment = input_str[brace_positions[pair_index - 1] + 1:open_pos]\n        outside_text.append(\"_\")\n        outside_text.append(outside_segment)\n        \n        pair_index += 2\n    \n    final_outside_segment = input_str[brace_positions[-1] + 1:]\n    outside_text.append(\"_\")\n    outside_text.append(final_outside_segment)\n    \n    cleaned_outside = \"\".join(outside_text)\n    cleaned_outside = cleaned_outside.replace(\"_\", \" \").strip().replace(\"\\\\s+\", \" \")\n    \n    outside_words = cleaned_outside.split(\" \")\n    for word in outside_words:\n        if len(word) > max_word_length:\n            max_word_length = len(word)\n    \n    print(f\"{max_word_length} {word_count_inside}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.030505417380482e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.048603225499391556, -0.011315220966935158, -0.0017037175130099058, -0.17090216279029846, -0.0001411338453181088, -0.5764614343643188, -0.031632717698812485, -0.00036125810584053397, -9.536738616588991e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.6331539882230572e-05, -0.4287717640399933, -4.887569048150908e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.4199192921514623e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00011097769311163574, -4.291525328881107e-06, -0.00013660451804753393, -0.6998254656791687, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.8596476365928538e-05, -5.